{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "avg-07-age-averages-through-time",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Age Averages Through Time",
    "description": "Treat age averages as changing age totals while carefully updating both elapsed time and family or class membership.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start with the unchanged-group rule that a mean age shifts by exactly the elapsed time, then prove it through total ages. Add membership changes one at a time: teacher joins, person leaves, replacement, birth and month-based changes. End with a marriage-and-birth timeline that requires separating the parents' pre-birth ageing from the child's present age.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 32,
    "sourceScope": "Teach that when the same people remain together, every age and therefore the average rises by the same number of years. Convert past averages to present totals, then handle a teacher joining, one person leaving, replacement, a birth, and average changes stated in months. Use short timelines and update the count whenever membership changes. Finish with a marriage-and-child timeline where the learner must separate years before the child was born from the child's present age."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn why age averages are really total-age stories with a clock running in the background.\n\nWhen the same people stay together, average age moves with time. When someone joins or leaves, the headcount changes too — and that is where the interesting questions begin.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Ages have one special feature: if the same people stay in the group, everyone grows older by the same amount.\n\nIf five people average 20 today, then four years later each is four years older.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So their average also rises by 4:\n\n20 + 4 = 24\n\nNo new total calculation is needed when the membership stays exactly the same.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
